<title>NORWAY: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF SUPER-G WINNER JOSEF STROBL.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF SUPER-G WINNER JOSEF STROBL.</headline>
<dateline>KVITFJELL, Norway 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a brief profile of the winner of a men's World Cup super-G on Sunday:</p>
<p>Name: Josef Strobl</p>
<p>Age: 22</p>
<p>Nationality: Austrian</p>
<p>World Cup wins: 3. Super-G - Kvitfjell (97), giant slalom - Park City (96), downhill - Val d'Isere (94)</p>
<p>Other facts: Second-youngest winner of a downhill World Cup race. Won first World Cup downhill he entered. Considered one of most promising all-rounders in powerful Austrian team.</p>
</text>
